This is kinda a vague question, but, basically:

Can anyone think of a good quest artifact for a neutral alignment
quest?  It doesn't have to fit with the description of the quest I
give below.

To add a bit more detail:  I've been fiddling around with the Nethack
source for a while now, adding new monsters, levels, artifacts, etc.
One of the overall projects I'm working on is adding Alignment-based
quests.  Basically, each one is a dungeon branch located somewhere
after the oracle level.  In order to get past a set of three
indestructible locked doors in the Valley of the Dead, the player
needs three alignment keys (Downwards level-teleport is blocked until
Ghennom is formally entered).

Since each alignment quest contains three keys, this amounts to
needing to thoroughly explore one of the quest branches, or partially
explore two or more of them.  The deeper levels of a quest are more
difficult, but the final level contains an artifact of the appropriate
alignment.

...

Obviously, I've been raiding SLASH'EM for code and ideas ;)

The Law quest runs upwards, starting with a trip up through a series
of maze levels to a library of sorts, followed by a trip through a
regimented orchard area to a castle.  The main law quest artifact is a
Silver spear (the Rod of Seven Parts (DnD)) that can cast a variety of
spells when invoked.  It's enchantment bonus decreases when these
spells are used and increases (to a max of +7) with normal use.  There
is also a mace which can be invoked to fire a barrage of iron balls.

The Chaos quest is a dark temple (which will look very familiar to
fans of the Final Fantasy series).  The Neutral quest starts with a
trip through a forested area to a cave.  Inside the cave is a town
populated by (hostile) golems, and a down staircase.  The main quest
artifacts are a set of Crystal Balls (ouch, my hernia!) that cast
spells when invoked.  There is also a unicorn horn that chaotic
players can use much like a scroll of scare monster.

The staircase leads to the underground banks of the Lethe river
(Lifted from the SLethe patch).  The banks of the Lethe are inhabited
by Mind Flayers and other dangerous creatures, and the final level is
Cthulhu's temple in Rlyeh (aka, re-purposed SLethe Sanctum level).
Cthulhu guards the Silver Key, the only artifact on this branch
currently, which allows branchport, teleport control, polymorph
control, and if wielded enables fast energy-regeneration.

However, the deeper parts of this quest are very difficult, and
Cthulhu himself is very dangerous, so it would be nice to offer a
second or third neutral artifact for reaching different parts of the
quest.  But I can't think of anything.


